    "contributingFactors": "• Alpha-fetoprotein and acetylcholinesterase may be falsely elevated if the sample is contaminated with fetal blood.\n• Bilirubin may be falsely elevated if the sample is contaminated with maternal hemoglobin or if meconium is present in the sample.\n• Bilirubin may be falsely low if the sample is exposed to light.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "• Possible complications include: amniotic fluid embolism, fetal injury, hemorrhage, infection, premature labor, Rh sensitization due to fetal bleeding into maternal circulation, and spontaneous abortion.\n• It is possible for some fetal blood cells to enter the mother’s bloodstream during the procedure. If the mother’s blood is Rh negative and the fetus’ is Rh positive, the mother may produce antibodies against the fetus. To avoid this, RhoGAM should be given to the mother.",
    "contraindications": "- Patients with abruptio placentae, incompetent cervix, placenta previa\n- Patients with a history of premature labor"
