    "contributingFactors": "• False-negative results may occur in patients with diabetes mellitus due to poorly compressible vessels.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "• Patients with PAOD require education on risk factor management, exercise, and pharmacologic treatment:\n• Treatment of hyperlipidemia with a target LDL of <100 mg/dL\n• Cessation of smoking\n• Exercise, preferably walking\n• Use of antiplatelet agents\n• If surgical intervention for PAOD is indicated, arteriography or magnetic resonance angiography is needed to determine the extent of the disease.\n• Primary care providers should consider evaluation for carotid artery stenosis in patients newly diagnosed with PAOD.",
