    "contributingFactors": "• Many variables influence the result, including skin thickness, temperature, location of incision, and presence of edema.\n• Platelet counts <100,000 mm3 and low hematocrit can alter the test result.\n• Drugs that may prolong the bleeding time: alcohol, antibiotics, anticoagulants, antineoplastics, nitroglycerin, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs), salicylates, thiazides, thrombolytics.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "• Possible complications include bleeding, scar formation, and skin infection at site of testing.",
