    "clinicalAlerts": "• Avoidance of errors is essential. Typically when blood is drawn for a type and crossmatch, a blood bank identification band is applied to the patient’s wrist. This band can be compared to blood products to be administered to the patient.\n• Follow institutional policy regarding identification of the patient prior to blood administration. Typically two health-care providers must verify that the blood group and Rh type of the recipient and donor are compatible and that the proper unit of blood is being used prior to blood administration.",
