    "contributingFactors": "• BMD results may be affected by nuclear scans within previous 3 days or barium studies within previous 7 to 10 days.\n• Metallic implants may affect the BMD imaging.\n• Absence of normal structures, such as after laminectomy, can affect BMD results",
    "clinicalAlerts": "Posttest\n• A computer printout of the images, along with T-scores, Z-scores, and interpretation are provided.\n• Report abnormal findings to the primary care provider. R Clinical Alerts\n• To help prevent osteoporosis, all adults should obtain adequate amounts of calcium (1200 mg/day) and vitamin D (400 to 800 IU/day), engage in regular weight-bearing exercise, and avoid tobacco smoking or alcohol abuse.\n• Follow-up BMD testing is recommended every 2 years.",
