    "description": "Cystometrography (CMG), also known as cystometry is used to evaluate detrusor muscle function and tone and to determine the cause of bladder dysfunction. The test involves the instillation of fluid and/or air into the patient’s bladder. Assessments are made of the patient’s neurologic sensations and muscular responses to this filling of the bladder. The patient’s voiding is also assessed for abnormalities. The results of this test are considered in conjunction with those of other urinary diagnostic tests, such as excretory urography and cystourethrography.\n\nCystourethrography involves the instillation of a contrast medium into the bladder through a urethral catheter. As the bladder fills, x-ray films are taken. The catheter is then removed and additional films are taken as the patient voids. This test is often used to evaluate patients who suffer from chronic urinary tract infections.",
