    "description": "Cystoscopy involves the insertion of a well-lubricated sheath into the urethra. During the procedure, a cystoscope is inserted through the sheath for direct visualization of the bladder. A urethroscope is used for examination of the bladder neck and the urethra. With the sheath in place, other instruments may be interchanged, allowing the physician to obtain tissue for biopsy, to resect lesions, to collect calculi, and to pass a ureteral catheter to the renal pelvis for pyelography. Indications for performing cystoscopy include recurrent urinary tract infections, dysuria with no known cause, hematuria, and bladder tumors.",
