    "contributingFactors": "• Excessive movement by the patient can blur images.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "• Use of an “open” MRI is an option for claustrophobic patients, however, the “closed” MRI provides a higher quality result.\n• Medication patches, such as nitroglycerin, contraception, or nicotine patches, must be removed prior to scanning. Many of these have a small metal wire inside and can cause thermal injury.\n• Some eye makeup has a metallic base and may cause fluttering of the eyelids. It is best to remove all eye makeup before having an MRI of the brain/head.\n• Patients with embedded wires, stimulators, or batteries cannot be scanned.",
