    "abnormalFindings": [],
    "contributingFactors": "• Exercise, smoking, menstruation, and dehydration can affect the results of microalbumin testing.",
    "clinicalAlerts": "• Because exercise, smoking, and menstruation can affect the results and albumin excretion can vary from day to day, an abnormal value should be repeated.\n• The diagnosis of persistent abnormal microalbumin excretion requires documentation of two of three consecutive abnormal values obtained on different days.\n• Confirmed, persistently elevated microalbumin levels should be treated with an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor titrated to normalization of microalbumin excretion. ARBs can also be used. The goal is to delay the progression of microalbuminuria to macroalbuminuria.",
