    "clinicalAlerts": "• If the rapid strep test is positive, the patient needs to be treated with an antibiotic, such as penicillin or, if allergic to penicillin, erythromycin.\n• If the rapid strep test is negative, a follow-up culture and sensitivity test is conducted to determine whether the rapid strep test result was a false negative result. It may take several days before the final culture report is available.\n• A positive test result does not differentiate between individuals with an active strep infection and those who are carriers of strep bacteria who may currently have a viral infection.",
