    "description": "Ultrasonography is a noninvasive method of diagnostic testing in which ultrasound waves are sent into the body with a small transducer pressed against the skin. The transducer then receives any returning sound waves, which are deflected back as they bounce off various structures. The transducer converts the returning sound waves into electric signals that are then transformed by a computer into a visual display on a monitor.\n\nWith scrotal ultrasound, visualization of the scrotum and its contents is made possible. This test is used to assess for scrotal masses and infections, evaluation of scrotal pain and trauma, locate undescended testicles, and provide monitoring for patients with previously diagnosed testicular cancer.",
