    "description": "Uroflowmetry is a noninvasive procedure which is used to detect dysfunctional voiding patterns. The test includes the measurement of the voiding duration, amount, and rate using a urine flowmeter, an instrument into which the patient voids. For\n\nthe most accurate evaluation of urine flow patterns, recording of each voiding for 2 to 3 days should be performed. Uroflowmetry is usually performed in conjunction with other urinary tract testing, such as cystometry. Although the urethral pressure profile test is more often used, uroflowmetry is useful for testing patients in whom urinary catheterization is contraindicated.",
