        "content": "- **Ankle-Brachial Index (ABI) Diagnostic Classification**:\n  - **Measurement**: Ratio of highest systolic blood pressure in the dorsalis pedis or posterior tibial artery divided by the highest brachial artery systolic pressure.\n  - **Diagnostic Tiers**:\n    - **1.00 – 1.40**: Normal lower extremity perfusion;\n    - **0.91 – 0.99**: Borderline perfusion;\n    - **0.71 – 0.90**: Mild peripheral arterial disease;\n    - **0.41 – 0.70**: Moderate PAD (typical intermittent claudication);\n    - **≤ 0.40**: Severe PAD / Critical limb ischemia (rest pain, nonhealing ulcers, tissue gangrene);\n    - **> 1.40**: Incompressible, severely calcified arteries (Mönckeberg sclerosis; common in long-standing diabetes or ESRD; requires Toe-Brachial Index [TBI])."
