        "relatedTests": "`Glucose, Blood` (P.280), `Glucose Tolerance Test` (P.283), `Glycohemoglobin` (P.286).",
        "content": "- **Diagnostic Criteria** (Requires repeat testing on a separate day unless classic hyperglycemia crisis is present):\n  1. **Fasting Plasma Glucose (FPG)**: ≥ 126 mg/dL (7.0 mmol/L) after fasting for ≥ 8 hours;\n  2. **2-Hour Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT)**: ≥ 200 mg/dL (11.1 mmol/L) following a 75-g anhydrous glucose load;\n  3. **Glycated Hemoglobin (HbA1c)**: ≥ 6.5% (48 mmol/mol) standardized to NGSP assay;\n  4. **Random Plasma Glucose**: ≥ 200 mg/dL (11.1 mmol/L) in a patient with classic symptoms of hyperglycemia (polyuria, polydipsia, unexplained weight loss) or hyperglycemic crisis."
