        "content": "- **Diagnostic Classification**:\n  - **Primary Overt Hypothyroidism**: Elevated TSH (> 10 mU/L) with decreased Free T4.\n  - **Subclinical Hypothyroidism**: Elevated TSH (4.5–10 mU/L) with normal Free T4.\n  - **Hashimoto Thyroiditis Confirmation**: Positive anti-thyroid peroxidase (anti-TPO) and anti-thyroglobulin (anti-Tg) antibodies.\n  - **Central Hypothyroidism**: Low or inappropriately normal TSH with low Free T4 (pituitary/hypothalamic pathology)."
