        "relatedTests": "`Urine Culture and Sensitivity` (P.594), `Urinalysis` (P.591).",
        "content": "- **Microbiologic Diagnostic Thresholds**:\n  - **Acute Uncomplicated Cystitis (Women with dysuria, urgency, frequency)**: Significant bacteriuria defined as **≥ 10³ CFU/mL** of a uropathogen (most commonly E. coli);\n  - **Acute Pyelonephritis (Fever, flank pain, costovertebral angle tenderness)**: **≥ 10⁴ CFU/mL**;\n  - **Catheter-Associated UTI**: **≥ 10⁵ CFU/mL** with signs/symptoms;\n  - **Suprapubic Aspiration**: Any bacterial growth (≥ 10² CFU/mL) is diagnostic."
