        "relatedTests": "`Rheumatoid Factor` (P.516), `Erythrocyte Sedimentation Rate` (P.245), `C-Reactive Protein` (P.200).",
        "content": "- **Diagnostic Criteria Scoring (Definite RA requires ≥ 6 of 10 points)**:\n  1. **Joint Involvement**: 1 large joint (0 pts); 2–10 large joints (1 pt); 1–3 small joints (2 pts); 4–10 small joints (3 pts); > 10 joints including ≥ 1 small joint (5 pts);\n  2. **Serology**: Negative RF and negative ACPA (0 pts); Low-positive RF or ACPA (2 pts); High-positive RF or ACPA (3 pts);\n  3. **Acute-Phase Reactants**: Normal CRP and normal ESR (0 pts); Abnormal CRP or abnormal ESR (1 pt);\n  4. **Duration of Symptoms**: < 6 weeks (0 pts); ≥ 6 weeks (1 pt).\n  - **Anti-Cyclic Citrullinated Peptide (Anti-CCP / ACPA)**: Most specific marker (> 95% specificity); predictive of aggressive, erosive joint destruction."
