        "relatedTests": "`Polysomnography` (P.477).",
        "content": "- **Diagnostic Polysomnography Criteria (Apnea-Hypopnea Index [AHI])**:\n  - Diagnosis established if **AHI ≥ 5 events/hour** with documented symptoms (excessive daytime sleepiness, loud snoring, witnessed apneas, nocturnal gasping, hypertension), OR **AHI ≥ 15 events/hour** regardless of symptoms;\n  - **Severity Stratification**:\n    - Mild: AHI 5–14.9;\n    - Moderate: AHI 15–29.9;\n    - Severe: AHI ≥ 30 events/hour."
