        "content": "- **Diagnostic Indications & Fetal Lung Maturity Indices**:\n  - Indications: Advanced maternal age (≥ 35 years at delivery), abnormal noninvasive aneuploidy screening, family history of genetic disorders, assessment of fetal infection.\n  - **Fetal Lung Maturity (Late Pregnancy Amniotic Fluid)**:\n    - **Lecithin/Sphingomyelin (L/S) Ratio**: L/S ratio **≥ 2.0** (≥ 2.5 in diabetic mothers) confirms fetal lung maturity and minimal risk of Neonatal Respiratory Distress Syndrome (RDS);\n    - **Phosphatidylglycerol (PG)**: Presence of PG confirms mature pulmonary surfactant production."
